  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3c793d2f08959c44eb266349fc49d2b8, type: 3}
  m_Name: RestSpotTuning
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::GameOff.Rest.RestSpotTuning
  moveSeconds: 0.6
  lookYaw: 70
  lookPitch: 30
  mouseDegrees: 0.08
  keyDegreesPerSecond: 60
  announcementSeconds: 14
  firstAnnouncementSeconds: 2.5
  subtitleSeconds: 6
  fastForwardSeconds: 4
  hallAnnouncements:
  - Attention, please. The observation deck closes at twenty-three hundred. Mind
    the step.
  - 'Passengers for the Aska shuttle: have your papers ready. Officers will not wait
    for you.'
  - Unattended luggage will be confiscated and inspected. Thank you for your cooperation.
  - KESTREL-9 thanks you for your patience. Your patience has been noted.
  - 'The diner remains closed until further notice. Today: no noodles.'
  - 'Lost and found: one ration card, one glove, one prosthetic finger. Ask station
    security.'
  eveningOver: It's late. The hall is empty. Time to sleep.
  portholeFov: 40
  thoughtDelay: 1
  thoughtsWell:
  - The lights over home are bright tonight. Somewhere under them Lena is doing her
    homework.
  - Pip asked if I can see them from up here. I can see the city. That's almost the
    same.
  - Everyone is fine. One more day, and then another.
  thoughtsWorried:
  - '{0} sounded tired in the letter. A little more food and it will pass.'
  - The city looks dimmer than yesterday. Probably just the glass.
  thoughtsSick:
  - '{0} needs medicine. I keep doing the sums, and they keep coming out short.'
  - I count the lights down there and lose track. I keep thinking of {0}.
  thoughtsCritical:
  - Half the lights are out down there. {0} is somewhere under them.
  - If {0} doesn't get medicine soon, there won't be another letter about it.
  thoughtsGrieving:
  - I used to find our block by its window. I don't look for it anymore.
  - '{0} is not down there anymore. The planet turns anyway.'
  letterJitter: 0.12
  letterTilt: 14
